From a8ec14c47391ed2b672383cfb371dcc74c450142 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ArnoldasMk <arnoldas.kanobi@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 23:22:31 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: reconstruct GQ5012BF1 st21nfc 2.2.0.19 source

Stock oracle: vendor ramdisk (platform.cpio) /lib/modules/st21nfc.ko,
version 2.2.0.19, sha256 5c5945457f8e3f37744c95a98075278134a328590d27e00d38dd8de8261078e8.

Against that shipped module the rebuild is 22/24 functions byte-identical,
23/24 size-identical, 33/33 data objects present, 54/54 import modversion
CRCs exact, .rodata/.data byte-exact, .rodata.str1.1 identical size and
string multiset, and modinfo (name/license/author/description/version/
alias/vermagic/depends) identical.

Deltas recovered on top of the NothingOSS 957dac1 donor:
- 24 error-path messages are pr_err, not pr_info;
- the two pidle_active_low messages are pr_info, not pr_debug;
- st21nfc_power_stats_idle_signal computes the active level as
  pidle_active_low ? (value == 0) : (value != 0);
- st21nfc_pstate_wq is static;
- probe's err_pidle_workqueue cleanup tests !IS_ERR (not IS_ERR_OR_NULL),
  which is what lets the three error gotos share the label.

Residual, both semantically equivalent to stock:
- st21nfc_dev_ioctl: identical instruction and relocation multisets, only
  two BL displacement fields differ (st21nfc_disable_irq /
  st21nfc_loc_set_polaritymode sit at different .text offsets);
- st21nfc_ping: +12 bytes, one error-path printk tail that stock merges
  into the shared _printk epilogue and the rebuild does not.
